Statutory Authority: Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021
Provision Reference: Section Rule 3
Statutory Text:
Rule 3. Due diligence by an intermediary.—(1) The intermediary shall observe due diligence while discharging its duties, including:
(a) The intermediary shall prominently publish on its website, mobile based application or both, the rules and regulations, privacy policy and user agreement for access or usage of its computer resource by any person;
(b) The intermediary shall inform its rules and regulations, privacy policy to user and shall cause user not to host, display, upload, modify, publish, transmit, store, update or share any information that belongs to another person and to which the user does not have any right, or is grossly harmful, harassing, blasphemous, defamatory, obscene, pornographic, pedophilic, invasive of another's privacy, or violates any law for the time being in force;
(c) An intermediary shall take all reasonable measures to secure its computer resource and information contained therein;
(d) The intermediary shall remove or disable access to unlawful content within 36 hours of receipt of actual knowledge in the form of a court order or notification by the Appropriate Government under section 79(3)(b) of the Act.

